 "jokes": [
  {
   "text": "Nirvana's folder in your Drive is still empty, {n}. Kurt would say “come as you are”, but maybe come with a chord sheet.",
   "date": "2026-10-12"
  },
  {
   "text": "Your tuner has seen things, {n}. Mostly a low E that thinks it's a D. Tap Listen and set it free.",
   "date": "2026-10-12"
  },
  {
   "text": "Green Day wrote three chords and sold millions. You know way more than three, {n}. No pressure.",
   "date": "2026-10-12"
  },
  {
   "text": "Tuna rhymes at 100 words a minute. Your chord changes can manage four a bar, {n}. Probably.",
   "date": "2026-10-12"
  },
  {
   "text": "Your guitar case has been closed so long it's started a podcast, {n}. Episode one: “Is anyone out there?”",
   "date": "2026-10-14"
  },
  {
   "text": "The tuner is warmed up, the capo is ready and the pick is right there. The only thing missing is you, {n}.",
   "date": "2026-10-14"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Beatles needed four people to make a band. You only need one guitar and 15 minutes, {n}.",
   "date": "2026-10-14"
  },
  {
   "text": "Brian May built his own guitar from a fireplace. You just have to pick yours up off the stand, {n}.",
   "date": "2026-10-14"
  },
  {
   "text": "Angus Young plays in a school uniform. You're allowed to practise in pyjamas, {n}. No excuses left.",
   "date": "2026-10-16"
  },
  {
   "text": "Jimmy Page played with a violin bow. You don't need one, {n}. Just the guitar and five spare minutes.",
   "date": "2026-10-16"
  },
  {
   "text": "Your chord sheets are in Drive, your guitar is on the stand and your thumbs are on your phone. Swap one of those, {n}.",
   "date": "2026-10-16"
  },
  {
   "text": "Hadag Nahash learned to groove one strum at a time. Your right hand is next in line, {n}.",
   "date": "2026-10-16"
  },
  {
   "text": "Kurt Cobain played a left-handed guitar upside down at times. You're allowed to play yours the right way up, {n}. Today would be nice.",
   "date": "2026-10-18"
  },
  {
   "text": "Your E string and your B string stopped talking to each other, {n}. Tap Listen and play peacemaker.",
   "date": "2026-10-18"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Edge built a whole sound out of delay pedals. Your practice routine is built out of delay too, {n}. Let's flip that.",
   "date": "2026-10-18"
  },
  {
   "text": "Rockfour toured the world on hard work and loud amps. You only need the hard work part tonight, {n}.",
   "date": "2026-10-18"
  },
  {
   "text": "Your pick has been on the coffee table so long it applied for residency, {n}. Put it back to work.",
   "date": "2026-10-20"
  },
  {
   "text": "Tom Morello makes his guitar sound like a DJ. You can start by making yours sound like a guitar, {n}.",
   "date": "2026-10-20"
  },
  {
   "text": "The F chord is not a wall, {n}. It's a door that buzzes. Push a little harder.",
   "date": "2026-10-20"
  },
  {
   "text": "Your string winder is bored, {n}. Change one string today and give it something to talk about.",
   "date": "2026-10-20"
  },
  {
   "text": "Bon Jovi was livin' on a prayer. You're livin' on one chord change a minute, {n}. Let's double it.",
   "date": "2026-10-22"
  },
  {
   "text": "Dave Grohl went from the drum stool to the front of the stage. You only need to get from the couch to the guitar, {n}.",
   "date": "2026-10-22"
  },
  {
   "text": "The dust on your guitar is thick enough for a slide solo, {n}. Wipe it off with a song instead.",
   "date": "2026-10-22"
  },
  {
   "text": "Strumming tip of the day, {n}: down, down, up, up, down, up. Scrolling is not part of the pattern.",
   "date": "2026-10-22"
  },
  {
   "text": "Tracy Chapman got a fast car. You got a whole new folder of her songs. Time to start the engine, {n}.",
   "date": "2026-10-24"
  },
  {
   "text": "Your capo has been clipped to the headstock so long it thinks it's a tuning peg, {n}. Give it a real job today.",
   "date": "2026-10-24"
  },
  {
   "text": "Your guitar stand is starting to look like a museum exhibit, {n}. Take the guitar off display and play it.",
   "date": "2026-10-24"
  },
  {
   "text": "Your strings said they're fine with being played every day, {n}. It's being ignored that makes them go flat.",
   "date": "2026-10-24"
  },
  {
   "text": "Mark Tremonti practises scales for hours. Your scales are still in the shop window, {n}. Five minutes today?",
   "date": "2026-10-26"
  },
  {
   "text": "Your metronome tried counting to four on its own and fell asleep at three, {n}. Wake it up with a song.",
   "date": "2026-10-26"
  },
  {
   "text": "The low E string says it's not too low to be asked for help, {n}. Give it a strum.",
   "date": "2026-10-26"
  },
  {
   "text": "Arik Einstein made simple chords sound like poetry. Your G chord is ready for its first verse, {n}.",
   "date": "2026-10-26"
  },
  {
   "text": "Oasis made “Don't Look Back in Anger” sound easy. Learn the first verse before dinner and make it look easy too, {n}.",
   "date": "2026-10-28"
  },
  {
   "text": "Your guitar strap has been on the hook so long it forgot what a shoulder feels like, {n}. Remind it.",
   "date": "2026-10-28"
  },
  {
   "text": "Your tuning pegs are spreading rumours that you only visit them when guests come over, {n}. Prove them wrong.",
   "date": "2026-10-28"
  },
  {
   "text": "The pick jar is full, the strings are shiny and the couch has had enough of you, {n}. Go play.",
   "date": "2026-10-28"
  },
  {
   "text": "Joe Satriani plays faster than the speed of thought. You only need to beat the speed of “maybe tomorrow”, {n}.",
   "date": "2026-10-30"
  },
  {
   "text": "Your guitar's warranty doesn't cover neglect, {n}. Luckily, ten minutes of playing fixes almost everything.",
   "date": "2026-10-30"
  },
  {
   "text": "Mosh Ben Ari found a whole world in a few simple chords. Grab yours and go looking, {n}.",
   "date": "2026-10-30"
  },
  {
   "text": "The open strings are E, A, D, G, B, E. The open invitation is right now, {n}.",
   "date": "2026-10-30"
  },
  {
   "text": "Power chords only need two fingers, {n}. That leaves eight fingers with no excuse at all.",
   "date": "2026-11-01"
  },
  {
   "text": "Hadag Nahash told everyone to get moving. Your fingers took it personally and stayed on the couch. Change that today, {n}.",
   "date": "2026-11-01"
  },
  {
   "text": "Your capo just asked for a promotion to fret five, {n}. Jack Johnson would approve. Go learn something breezy.",
   "date": "2026-11-01"
  },
  {
   "text": "Fun fact: diminished chords sound tense because they've been waiting for you to practise them, {n}.",
   "date": "2026-11-01"
  },
  {
   "text": "Johnny Marr can make one guitar sound like three. You only need to make yours sound like one today, {n}.",
   "date": "2026-11-03"
  },
  {
   "text": "Your capo, picks and tuner held a meeting about you, {n}. There was only one item on the agenda: “When?”",
   "date": "2026-11-03"
  },
  {
   "text": "Kaveret made “Yo Ya” sound like the easiest thing in the world. Your Am to Dm change can borrow that attitude today, {n}.",
   "date": "2026-11-03"
  },
  {
   "text": "The G string hummed a little when you walked past, {n}. In guitar, that means “pick me up”.",
   "date": "2026-11-03"
  },
  {
   "text": "Jack White made a whole band out of two people. Tonight's rehearsal only needs one person and one guitar, {n}.",
   "date": "2026-11-05"
  },
  {
   "text": "Your setlist for tonight has exactly one song on it, {n}. It's called “Pick Up the Guitar”.",
   "date": "2026-11-05"
  },
  {
   "text": "Carlos Santana can make one note cry. You can start by making one chord ring clean, {n}.",
   "date": "2026-11-05"
  },
  {
   "text": "Danny Sanderson hides clever little guitar fills in every song. Learn one today and save it for the next party, {n}.",
   "date": "2026-11-05"
  },
  {
   "text": "Neil Young has been rocking in the free world for decades. You only need to rock for twenty minutes before dinner, {n}.",
   "date": "2026-11-07"
  },
  {
   "text": "Your chord sheets have been sitting in Drive so long they started reading each other, {n}. Give them an audience.",
   "date": "2026-11-07"
  },
  {
   "text": "The Stones sang that time is on their side. It's on yours too, {n}, but only if you spend it with the guitar.",
   "date": "2026-11-07"
  },
  {
   "text": "Your fretboard has 22 frets and you've met maybe five of them, {n}. Today, say hello to a new one.",
   "date": "2026-11-07"
  },
  {
   "text": "Joni Mitchell invented dozens of tunings. You only need to finish one, {n}. Tap Listen.",
   "date": "2026-11-09"
  },
  {
   "text": "Your guitar has six strings and zero patience left for excuses, {n}. Ten minutes, starts now.",
   "date": "2026-11-09"
  },
  {
   "text": "Rockfour sang in English for the world. Your fingers only need to speak fluent C major tonight, {n}.",
   "date": "2026-11-09"
  },
  {
   "text": "Your B string is still flat from last week, {n}. It's not sulking, it's waiting for you.",
   "date": "2026-11-09"
  },
  {
   "text": "Dave Grohl tunes his low E down to D and the whole room shakes. Today you can try it too, {n}. Just tune it back afterwards.",
   "date": "2026-11-11"
  },
  {
   "text": "Your fingerpicking hand has been keeping score, {n}: thumb 12, index 3, ring finger 0. Time to even things out.",
   "date": "2026-11-11"
  },
  {
   "text": "The slash in G/B isn't a typo, {n}. It's the bass note asking you to stop ignoring it.",
   "date": "2026-11-11"
  },
  {
   "text": "Shlomo Artzi changes key mid-song and nobody panics. You can survive one new chord tonight, {n}.",
   "date": "2026-11-11"
  }
 ],
 "jokesDate": "2026-11-11"
}